{
  "_doc": "The season registry (docs/design/brand/seasons/README.md 'How to add a season'). ONE source, copied byte-for-byte to apps/ios/Wordocious/Resources/season-registry.json and apps/android/app/src/main/assets/season-registry.json (apps/web/lib/season-registry.test.ts checks the copies). Windows live in core SEASON_WINDOWS (×3 ports, level-season-fixtures.json) and must list the same ids. Slots name shipped art (web /art/<name>.webp, iOS image set <name>, Android drawable <name with _>); 'titles' and 'walls' map the NORMAL art name to the seasonal one ('*' = prefix); a light-mode wall twin '<name>-light' wins in light mode. 'castSize' + 'castTrim' = the skins' square size and alpha boxes [x0, y0, x1, y1] (alpha > 8), so the cast row frames any season's skins. Any missing slot or unshipped file falls back to the normal art. 'surfaces' (optional) recolors the app's windows during the season: tone ('dark' = light on-card + on-wall text, dark system chrome / status bar), card + cardOpacity (page cards, game board panel), hero + heroOpacity (the Home hero card), raised (chips inside cards), cap (the game cards' drip trim stops, top -> base; capTint mixes each game's own color into the middle stop), glow (the cards' soft lift color), text / textMuted / textSecondary (on-card ink), headline (the hero greeting lettering: top, bottom, deep, nameTop, nameBottom), bannerGlow (a soft glow behind the hero's banner art) and cobweb (the hero's top-corner web ink; absent = none). The DEBUG key debug-season-surfaces = 'off' (web ?surfaces=off) turns the surfaces off for an A/B (perf, contrast) while the season art stays. Any missing surface slot keeps the normal look. 'stage' (10-16, optional) = the Home curtain-stage card art behind the headline zone (core CELEBRATION_STAGE pool geometry, 1586 x 992); absent or unshipped = the plain card. Whether a season is LIVE for the public is core SEASON_WINDOWS[].ready (x3 ports): a not-ready season is listed for the admin Season preview only. 'extras' may also map the sweep / flawless celebration SCENE art itself ('art-scene-sweep-broom' / 'art-scene-flawless-star' -> a costumed scene, e.g. celebrate-h-scene-flawless-star); when the season scene is present the crown overlay is NOT drawn (the scene carries its own headwear: founder 10-16, no loose hats on cast art). TIME OF DAY (10-16, docs/design/brand/seasons/time-of-day/NOTES.md v2; core TimeOfDay, ×3 ports): while a season shows, the wall, the Home stage and the window surfaces follow the device's LOCAL clock (morning 5-10, day 10-16, evening 16-19, night 19-5). A 'walls' value or the 'stage' may be an art name (the same at every time) OR an object {night, morning, day, evening}: night is the base look and the fallback whenever a time's key is missing or its file doesn't ship. 'surfaces.tod.<morning|day|evening>' is a PARTIAL override of the base surfaces (= night): any key present replaces the base for that time; 'tone' there only flips the ON-WALL ink ('light' = dark ink on the wall chrome, the cards keep their light ink), never the card tone. Outside a season nothing changes. Per-time art names: <name>-<time> (night = <name>).",
